let __v_1840 = Value::from("Cut the stalk off and halve it lengthways, then scrape the seeds and the pale pith out with the tip of a knife or a teaspoon - that pith is where most of the heat sits, so take it out too if you want the chilli mild. Slice it on a board, not in your hand, and keep your hands away from your eyes and your mouth. Wash the board, the knife and your hands in cold water and soap straight after: the oil that burns is not washed off by rinsing. If your hands do burn, rub them with oil then wash again, or soak them in milk, not water.");
frame.store("_CHILLI_SEEDS", __v_1840.clone())?;
let __v_1841 = Value::from("Cut the crown off and score the skin down the ridges, then break it open in a bowl of water and knock the seeds out with a wooden spoon: the seeds sink, the pith and the membrane float and you can skim them off. Doing it under water is what stops the juice reaching your shirt, and it is much quicker than picking them out.");
frame.store("_POMEGRANATE_SEEDS", __v_1841.clone())?;
let __v_1842 = Value::from("Halve it across the middle, not top to bottom, and squeeze or scoop the seeds out with a finger or a teaspoon. The jelly round them is the flavour, so keep it if you are cooking; for a sandwich or a salad, a sieve catches the juice and you can salt the halves and leave them upside down for ten minutes instead.");
frame.store("_TOMATO_SEEDS", __v_1842.clone())?;
let __v_1843 = Value::from("Halve it lengthways and run a teaspoon down the middle to scoop the watery seeds out - a grapefruit spoon has the right edge for it. Salt the halves and leave them face down for fifteen minutes afterwards and the water comes out too, which is what a soggy sandwich is.");
frame.store("_CUCUMBER_SEEDS", __v_1843.clone())?;
let __v_1844 = Value::from("Halve it and scoop the seeds out with a spoon, then rinse the last of the strings off under the tap. A watermelon is easier cut into wedges and the seeds flicked out with the tip of a knife, and if you want it neat, cut it in slices and stamp the seeds out with a small round cutter.");
frame.store("_MELON_SEEDS", __v_1844.clone())?;
let __v_1845 = Value::from("Halve it and scoop the strings and seeds out with a metal spoon, working round the edge towards the middle. Keep the seeds: rinse them, toss in a little oil and salt and roast them at 180C for 10 to 15 minutes.");
