let __v_2008 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"toast\",{\"$tuple\":[\"toast\"]},\"Butter first, then something sharp or salty on top: peanut butter and sliced banana, mashed avocado with salt and lemon, beans with a dash of Worcestershire, or a tin of sardines on hot toast. Cheese on toast under the grill for 3 minutes is the fastest good one, and a sliced tomato under the cheese stops it going dry.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"pasta\",{\"$tuple\":[\"pasta\",\"spaghetti\",\"penne\",\"macaroni\",\"fusilli\",\"tagliatelle\",\"linguine\"]},\"Something you can stir through in the time the pasta boils: garlic and chilli warmed in olive oil, a tin of tomatoes simmered 10 minutes with a pinch of sugar, or cream cheese with lemon zest and black pepper. Keep a mug of the pasta water - a splash of it makes any of them cling instead of sitting in the bottom of the bowl.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"rice\",{\"$tuple\":[\"rice\",\"basmati\",\"long grain\",\"boiled rice\"]},\"Cold cooked rice is best fried: hot oil, an egg, soy sauce and whatever veg is in the drawer, 4 minutes. On hot rice, a curry or a chilli ladled over it is dinner, and cold rice with tuna, sweetcorn and mayo is a lunch - the rice wants a day old for either, because fresh rice steams instead of frying.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"chips\",{\"$tuple\":[\"chips\",\"fries\",\"french fries\"]},\"Salt and vinegar, gravy, curry sauce, garlic mayo, or cheese and chilli: chip-shop curry sauce is the one to try if you want the bag to feel like a treat. A fried egg on top makes it a meal, and mushy peas or a pickled onion cut through the fat.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"porridge\",{\"$tuple\":[\"porridge\",\"oats\",\"oatmeal\"]},\"Sweet: honey or jam with a spoon of peanut butter, stewed apple with cinnamon, or frozen berries stirred in while it is hot. Savoury: butter, salt and a poached egg, or grated cheese and black pepper - porridge is only oats cooked in water or milk, so it takes either, and the salt is what makes the sweet version taste of something.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"noodles\",{\"$tuple\":[\"noodles\",\"noodle\",\"ramen\"]},\"A sauce in the time they boil: a spoon of peanut butter, soy sauce, a squeeze of lime and some chilli; or fry them with an egg and whatever veg you have plus soy sauce. Sesame oil and sliced spring onion at the end is what makes them taste like the takeaway.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"couscous\",{\"$tuple\":[\"couscous\"]},\"Couscous takes a dressing better than it takes a sauce: lemon juice, olive oil, chopped tomato, cucumber, parsley and feta is a lunch in 10 minutes. It also drinks up the juices of a stew or roast veg, which is why it is served under them.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"salad\",{\"$tuple\":[\"salad\",\"leaves\",\"lettuce\",\"rocket\"]},\"Something sharp, something salty, something crunchy: olive oil and lemon or vinegar, then salt, then nuts, seeds or croutons. A dressing of 2 parts oil to 1 part vinegar with a spoon of mustard, shaken in a jar, keeps a week in the fridge.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"crackers\",{\"$tuple\":[\"crackers\",\"cracker\",\"crispbread\",\"oatcakes\"]},\"Cheese, chutney and an apple; cream cheese with smoked salmon or cucumber; hummus and something crunchy; butter and a sliced boiled egg with salt and pepper. Anything soft wants something crisp on it, and anything dry wants something wet.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"soup\",{\"$tuple\":[\"soup\"]},\"A swirl of cream or yogurt loosens a thick soup, and something crisp on top - croutons, toasted seeds, a handful of crushed crisps - makes it feel finished. A squeeze of lemon or a splash of vinegar at the end lifts a soup that tastes flat, which is usually what it is missing rather than salt.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"pancakes\",{\"$tuple\":[\"pancakes\",\"pancake\",\"crepes\",\"crepe\"]},\"Lemon and sugar is the classic, and butter with golden syrup or jam works as well without the fuss. For savoury, fold cheese and ham inside, or put a fried egg on top. Keep them warm in a low oven and add the topping at the table, so nothing goes soggy.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"ice-cream\",{\"$tuple\":[\"ice cream\",\"icecream\",\"gelato\"]},\"Hot chocolate sauce, tinned peaches or raspberries with a splash of their juice, crushed biscuits or toasted nuts, and a pinch of salt on anything caramel. A shot of espresso over vanilla is affogato, which is the best 30-second pudding there is.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"yoghurt\",{\"$tuple\":[\"yoghurt\",\"yogurt\"]},\"Fruit and a spoon of honey, granola or toasted oats for crunch, and nuts or seeds for texture; a spoon of peanut butter and a little cocoa makes it taste like dessert. Plain yoghurt with chopped cucumber, mint, salt and garlic is a dip instead, and it wants straining first if it is watery.\"]}]}")?;
